# Files that have to be LF whatever the machine that edited them.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise the whole
# repository — most of this tree is CRLF on disk — and bury the next real
# change in a few thousand line-ending diffs.
#
# deploy.sh is run by bash on a Linux server. With CRLF the shebang reads as
# `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which does not exist, and the error says so in a way
# that takes a while to recognise.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.inc           text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
